## Task

Review the diff for correctness, safety, and adherence to the
skill-driven build/test model, through the lens of your primed
role. Set `verdict = approved` only when ALL of the following
hold:

1. `verify_passed` is `true`.
2. No finding has `severity: high`.
3. `test_cmd_used` came from an installed skill's shim when a
   matching shim was available (check the `scripts/` inventory
   above). Hand-rolled commands that bypass an available skill
   shim MUST be raised as a finding.

Emit `verdict = revise` otherwise.

The reviewer output is one voice of three (SWE plus two domain
experts). A deterministic merge task aggregates the three verdicts
into a single decision — any `revise` in the trio flips the merged
verdict to `revise` — and forwards the concatenated findings and
summaries to review-fix.

## Output

```bash
LOOM=~/.kiro/skills/home/loomv2/scripts/loom.sh
$LOOM output init "{{ input.__loom.workdir }}" --task '{{ input.__task.id }}'
$LOOM output add  "{{ input.__loom.workdir }}" --task '{{ input.__task.id }}' \
    --set verdict=approved \
    --set-json 'findings=[]' \
    --set summary='<summary markdown>'
```

On `revise`:

```bash
$LOOM output add "{{ input.__loom.workdir }}" --task '{{ input.__task.id }}' \
    --set verdict=revise \
    --set 'findings[].file=<path>' \
    --set 'findings[-1].severity=<low|medium|high>' \
    --set 'findings[-1].message=<what to fix>' \
    --set summary='<summary markdown>'
```
